# What must never reach the repository.
#
# This file is the last line of defence, not the first: a key that is pasted
# into a source file is still a leaked key, and git history cannot be edited
# once it is pushed. The rule is that credentials live in .env locally and in
# the deployment's environment settings on Vercel — never in a file, ever.
#
# Adding a pattern here does NOT untrack a file that is already committed.
# Check with `git ls-files` before trusting a new rule.

# --- Build output and dependencies ----------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
.vite
.cache
.turbo
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Local environment, including every credential the app uses ------------
# .env holds the Supabase service-role key and the HB+ admin token. Both are
# full-power credentials; neither is a VITE_ variable, so neither reaches the
# browser, and neither may reach git.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
.envrc
env.local
# Scratch copies made while loading variables into a host. These have a habit
# of being written next to the project and forgotten.
vercel-env*.txt
*-env-vars*.txt

# --- Keys, certificates and service accounts -------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.asc
*.gpg
*.secret
*.secrets
secrets*.json
credentials*.json
service-account*.json
*-service-account*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
gcp-*.json
# npm and curl keep auth tokens in these.
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass

# --- Supabase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The whole directory is kept out: schema, migrations, patches and the CLI's
# local state. Apply the SQL from your own copy through the Supabase SQL
# editor. The two exceptions are the notes on how to do that and the seed
# script, both of which read their credentials from the environment and carry
# none of their own.
supabase/*
!supabase/README.md
!supabase/seed.mjs
.supabase
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

# Every .sql file, wherever it is written. The schema describes the shape of
# live payroll data, and a patch written in a hurry in the project root is the
# one that gets committed by accident.
*.sql
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.bak
*.backup

# --- Anything carrying coaches' personal data ------------------------------
# Payslips, pay exports and roster imports hold salaries, bank details, PAN
# and addresses. None of it belongs in a repository, and a repository is
# where exports land by default.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
exports/
payslips/

# --- Host and tooling state -------------------------------------------------
.vercel
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.gemini
.agents
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
